; AI-generated: this file was written by Claude, an AI model.

; The traditional flapping bird, after the 17 steps of Nick Robinson's
; diagram [robinson2025bird]. The diagram holds the paper as a diamond and
; turns the model over at step 9 to fold the back; the program folds the
; back from the front with mountain folds instead. Steps 5 to 7 and step 10
; crease lines and unfold them again; a flat state needs no precrease, so
; the program folds steps 8 and 11 along those lines directly, the way the
; crane does [ida2020, Fig. 7.19].
;
; The kernel folds the model through step 13. Step 14 does not fold yet
; (#208): it is written out below, commented, with the error it gives, and
; steps 15 to 17 wait on it. The last state the program reaches is the
; diagram's picture at step 14.

paper square

; steps 1 and 3 crease the diagonals and the midlines, with the paper
; turned over between them (step 2), so the two sets fold in opposite
; directions when step 4 collapses them
mark (through .a .c) as --ac                ; step 1
mark (through .b .d) as --bd                ; step 1
mark (map --ab onto --cd) as --h            ; step 3
mark (map --da onto --bc) as --v            ; step 3

; step 4: collapse into the square base. .q and .r only name the quarters
; at .a and .b, so that the quarter at .a comes to lie over the one at .b;
; the quarter at .c stays where it lies, and its corner is the open end
; where all four corners meet
.q = free on --ab from .a at 1/4
.r = free on --ab from .b at 1/4
flatten (--h & --bc) (--v & --cd) (--h & --da) (--v & --ab) (--bd & .b) (--bd & .d) (.q over .r) (staying .c) (toward .q)    ; step 4

.o = --h * --v                              ; the paper center, the closed end
--mid = (through .c .o)                     ; center line of the base

; step 8, the petal fold of the front: each front side corner reversed
; inside along the line of step 5, which takes the raw edge onto the center
; line, then the bottom corner .a lifted along the line of step 6, the
; perpendicular to the center line through the point where the side corners
; landed. `up to` names the center face of the flap; the side corners
; reversed beneath it follow.
.sr = --ab * --v
.sl = --da * --h
reverse (map .sr onto --mid through .c) as --rsr      ; step 8
reverse (map .sl onto --mid through .c) as --rsl      ; step 8
fold (perp --mid through .sr) (moving .a) (up to #[.a .o]) as --pf     ; step 8

; step 11, the petal fold of the back, the same three folds behind
.br = --bc * --h
.bl = --cd * --v
reverse (map .br onto --mid through .c) as --rbr      ; step 11
reverse (map .bl onto --mid through .c) as --rbl      ; step 11
fold (perp --mid through .sr) (moving .c) (up to #[.c .o]) (mountain) as --pb      ; step 11

; step 12 turns the front left flap over to the right like the page of a
; book, then the back one to the left. Each page holds half of a petal and
; one leg, the flap whose tip is .d in front and .b behind. The crease runs
; along the center line: it folds the petal in half and opens the leg flat.
; `up to` names the flap that holds the leg's tip, a side vertex and the
; paper center. .kl, .kr, .kh and .kv are the four side vertices of the
; base, where the lines of steps 5 and 6 meet.
.kl = --rsl * --pf
.kr = --rsr * --pf
.kh = --rbr * --pb
.kv = --rbl * --pb
fold (through .c .o) (moving .kl) (up to #[.d .kl .o]) as --bkf      ; step 12, front
fold (through .c .o) (moving .kh) (up to #[.b .kh .o]) (mountain) as --bkb      ; step 12, back

; step 13: the legs, now the flaps at the bottom, folded up along the line
; of step 6, the front one in front and the back one behind. They become
; the wings.
fold (perp --mid through .sr) (moving .d) (up to #[.d .kl .o]) as --wf      ; step 13, front
fold (perp --mid through .sr) (moving .b) (up to #[.b .kh .o]) (mountain) as --wb      ; step 13, back

; step 14 pulls the half petal that stands between the wings on the left
; out and flattens it as the tail, so that its bottom edge lines up with
; the edge at the foot of the wing. That turns the flap about the bottom
; center of the body, the point .sr, by 45 degrees, and a turn is two
; reflections: the half petal folded back down along the line of step 6,
; then reversed up along the perpendicular to its outer edge through .sr,
; the crease that puts that edge in line. The first of the two fails: the
; line lies along the bottom edge of the model.
;
; .pm = --pf * --bkf
; fold (perp --mid through .sr) (moving .a) (up to #[.a .kl .pm]) as --ut       ; step 14
;   error: this fold is degenerate: the crease line lies along the edge of
;   the paper and does not separate it into two flaps to reflect
; reverse (perp --rsl & .a through .sr) (moving .a) as --tail                   ; step 14
;
; Folded before step 13, while the line still crosses the model, the same
; fold takes the other half petal along with it. A single reverse of the
; upright half petal, from .sr to the middle of its outer edge, folds and
; puts the tip at 45 degrees, but keeps the whole flap above the line of
; step 6, where the diagram shows part of it below that line from step 15
; on.
;
; Step 15 pulls out the half petal on the right as the neck, step 16
; creases the head at a point the diagram leaves to the eye, and step 17
; reverses the head along that crease.

; turned the way the diagram draws the bird from step 14 to the end: the
; bottom center of the body down, the wing tips up
@orient .sr .d up

; assert steps = 11

; Pieces of the marks of steps 1 and 3 lie flat in this state, so the 24
; faces make 20 flaps; a test in test_e2e.ml counts them.
; assert faces = 24

; all four corners of the square meet at the top: the tips of the two
; wings and of the two half petals between them
; assert .a = .c
; assert .b = .d
; assert .a = .b
; assert .o = (1/2, 1/2)

; the outline is a triangle on the line of step 6: the four side corners
; meet at its middle, and the side vertices lie in pairs at its two ends
; assert .sr = .sl
; assert .sr = .br
; assert .sr = .bl
; assert .kl = .kr
; assert .kh = .kv
